Reading it: `caught` is what the layer is for, but on its own it proves
nothing — a layer that shouts contradiction at everything scores 100%.
Read it against the false-alarm row, which is what such a layer costs.
The two miss rows split the failures by cause, which is the part that
decides anything: a claim whose target was never retrieved is not a
judgment the model got wrong, it is one the model never saw. 100% of
misses were the model's, so that is the ceiling on what swapping the
NLI model could recover. The gate table asks the other question —
whether the two populations separate by confidence at all, and so
whether this is fixable without changing the model.

